{"body":"The conjecture tests open:creib.forge.conformance.oracle._grounding_kernel. Its documented rule requires no relaxation, so a span must occur in the document exactly as written. The first reply has span 'a  b' in document 'a b', which should be SPAN_NOT_IN_DOCUMENT; the second has span 'a b' in document 'a b', which should be GROUNDED. The function is reported to normalise whitespace in _span_occurs even with empty relaxations, returning GROUNDED for both, so it fails to tell apart a pair the rule requires to differ. I read this as a moves expectation.","commitments":"{\"kernel\":\"open:creib.forge.conformance.oracle._grounding_kernel\",\"expect\":\"moves\"}"}